# AIDE SESSION

Cold-start protocol for agents reorienting on this project. This is a
snapshot of the current architectural intent and the anti-regression
invariants every build phase must hold. It is NOT historical commentary —
superseded design decisions are cut, not annotated.

## State summary (set 2026-10-26, v0.14.0 released; site live)

2026-10-26 (latest, v0.14.0 released): After the pinned-behind task's QA, an end-to-end test ran the new code as a fake 0.12.0 server over real MCP stdio (pinned cmd /c npx with CRLF+tabs: aide_info behind 0.12.0→0.13.1, 3 versions, 3 highlights; pin move changed exactly 2 bytes; unpinned, global, missing entry, invalid input, offline all correct), a real npx pre-fetch (`sync --help` → Usage:, exit 2; nonexistent version → exit 1, no Usage:), and headless `claude -p /aide` boots; the headless agent skipped the notice, so SKILL.md Step 3.1 was changed to put the notice inside the AskUserQuestion question text (or write it before the first upgrade call when the session cannot ask) and lead the outcome message with it — committed 7367af2. The user then drove an interactive /aide boot in a test project (fake 0.12.0 linked into its node_modules so the project's own npx entry ran the new code): the upgrade question carried the notice, "Upgrade (Recommended)" was answered, v0.13.1 was pre-fetched, the pin moved @0.12.0→@0.13.1 (only those bytes), and boot halted for a new session. CHANGELOG [Unreleased] moved under `## [0.14.0] - 2026-10-26`; `node scripts/publish.mjs minor` committed b62c696 ("0.14.0: …"), tagged v0.14.0 and pushed main (bf2e89e..b62c696, carrying c6af03e, 12a5c3a, 5bb3c12, 7367af2). Publish and CI workflows green; npm serves 0.14.0; global install 0.14.0. aidemd.dev synced headless to 0.14.0 (site commit 0c3fa7d: .aide/docs/changelog.md, .aide/versions.json, commands upgrade.md + brain.md, skills aide SKILL.md), deploy green; its brainMigration still lists kanban-index. Side effect during test setup: an `npm install` run from the test folder (no package.json there) landed in the user's home folder and created C:\Users\bestb\node_modules (all entries from 16:59 2026-10-26); the junction inside it was removed safely, but deleting the folder was blocked by the auto-mode classifier — the user was asked to delete it themselves.

2026-10-26 (earlier, pinned-behind task done; unreleased): Built and QA passed. aide_info `behind` now covers every launch (global or npx, pinned or not), judged on the running serverVersion; shape `{ installed, latest, launch, versionsBehind, highlights }`; one registry request (registry.npmjs.org abbreviated metadata, 1.5 s) gives latest + version list; highlights (≤3, one line ≤120 chars, Added→Fixed→Changed, newest first, no [migration]) from https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@aidemd-mcp/server@<latest>/CHANGELOG.md (2 s), only when behind; any failure silent. `outdated` unchanged (judged against the running server). aide_upgrade gained `targetVersion` (exact x.y.z; valid with no category or `mcp`): detection reports `pinMove: { from, to }` for a local aide entry whose pin is older/missing/non-exact (never a prescription); `category: "mcp"` + targetVersion makes the tool rewrite only the version token in .mcp.json (yaml.parseDocument byte range, re-verified with changesOnlyThePin, refuses on a changed pin or unsafe edit); never moves a pin ahead of the target back (prerelease ahead judged by x.y.z — fix-loop step 6); global/custom/missing/legacy-key paths unchanged; no-target results identical to before. readNpxPackageSpec + isOlderVersion lifted to src/service/install/shared (provisionBrain uses them). Prose by the main agent: /aide skill boot Step 3 (behind → short notice → global `npm i -g`, local: pre-fetch `npx -y @aidemd-mcp/server@{latest} sync --help` (exits 2 by design; success = prints `Usage:`), only then `aide_upgrade({ category: "mcp", targetVersion })`, then halt for a new session; outdated → /aide:upgrade → halt for a new session if anything changed); /aide:upgrade mcp handling + final new-session note; aide_info and aide_upgrade descriptions in src/index.ts; CHANGELOG [Unreleased] Added/Changed/Fixed (no [migration]: no file format change). Specs: src/tools/info/.aide frontmatter re-amended + Strategy body (7 decisions); src/tools/upgrade/.aide desired[5]/undesired[5] amended + body updated. Two early plans (src/service/install, provisionBrain lift for info) abandoned with the user's OK and removed. QA: info passed with notes (no todo); upgrade QA found 2 items (prose tripped retiredVocabulary hand-edit rule → reworded to "yourself"; prerelease pin ahead moved down → isPinBehind step 6), both fixed, re-QA PASS; full suite 3118/3119 (only the known singleSource load flake, passes alone), tsc clean. All plans/briefs/todo recorded completed and removed via aide_cleanup (src/tools/upgrade, src/tools/info, src/types, src/service/install, src/service/install/provisionBrain, src). Retro: process/retro/2026-10-26-aidemd-pinned-behind-and-pin-move.md.

