late section edit — pipeline, and the old fingerprint must be appended so existing configs are still recognized) and this repo's .aide/config/brain.aide kanban-hub section (changes only through /aide:brain config).

2026-10-26 (Read-entry addressing fix): diagnosed why an implementor skipped playbook entries. Root cause: plans write `Read:` entries in a shape the brain's read tool rejects — e.g. `coding-playbook/workflow/type-system` with no `.md`, or `…/conventions#Early Returns Over Nesting` with an anchor — so the first read fails "File not found"; most implementors recovered (added .md / browsed), one fell back on the surrounding code's style; nothing asked for a report and nobody checked. User direction: the architect must write the path exactly as the tool requires, generically, so no prose changes per MCP integration. Fix (prose by the main agent, uncommitted at the time of writing): aide-architect and aide-auditor write each Read entry as the exact address they loaded it with, copied from their own successful read (never retyped from memory, docs examples or links); sections named in words, never as anchors. plan-aide.md rule + examples rewritten as placeholders (`<address of … entry>`). aide-implementor: pass addresses through unchanged; an entry that won't load is found via the brain's navigation or the step stops; never substitute nearby code style; new "Playbook entries" item in its return (loaded / not loaded); fix mode loads entries too. /aide skill Stage 5 step 3 and /aide:build check that report and re-run a step whose entries weren't loaded (or send a bad address back to the architect). CHANGELOG [Unreleased] Fixed bullet. Guard/install/upgrade tests green (1219). The user later decided against an automatic post-QA check (see latest).

