2026-10-25 (earlier, Stage 4): The user confirmed the src/tools/scaffold/.aide frontmatter, and that agents never choose the name (research after intent is already handled by scaffold's rename). Stage 4: aide-architect wrote two Shape B plans, both proposed, no brief: src/tools/scaffold/plan.aide (3 steps; step 3 has 3a–3d) and src/plan.aide (1 step: a test in src/index.test.ts pinning the aide_scaffold registered description — it must contain `.aide/intent.aide`, `project root intent spec` and `research.aide`; build it only after the main agent edits that description). Planning found a second bug, confirmed in a temp project: existingAideFiles matches any name ending in `.aide`, so at directory "." it counts the `.aide/` folder as a spec — type intent reports a false skip, and type research/both RENAMES the whole `.aide/` folder to `intent.aide/`. Key plan decisions are in decision #41. Prose follow-ups for the main agent: the src/index.ts aide_scaffold description; CHANGELOG [Unreleased] Fixed + [migration] (Detect: .aide/.aide exists and .aide/intent.aide does not; Migrate: aide_scaffold({ directory: ".aide", type: "intent" }); Confirm: once, as a batch); the aide-spec.md bootstrapping paragraph; the aide-spec-writer naming bullets. Awaiting the user's plan approval. The `.aide/` folder rename bug was then traced and reproduced in production. The code dates from c123937 (2026-04-09, "Implement all MCP tools and lib modules with tests"), so every published version from v0.3.1 to v0.12.0 has it. Reproduced with the globally installed 0.12.0 dist in a temp project: `aide_scaffold({ directory: ".", type: "research" })` printed "Renamed .aide → intent.aide / Created research.aide" and left the project root holding `intent.aide/` (the whole methodology folder, with docs/ and session.aide inside, contents intact) plus `research.aide`. Nothing is deleted — the folder is moved — so an affected project recovers by renaming `intent.aide/` back to `.aide/`. Trigger: type research or both with directory "." (project-root research); type intent at "." only reports a false skip. The fix is already in the proposed src/tools/scaffold plan.

