- The server reports its version as "0.2.0" in MCP serverInfo — a stale hard-coded label.
- aidemd.dev's `docs:verify` expects 33 files, counts 42 — stale count in the site's script.
- Retro rules for the architect agent (always include `foundations/conventions` in step Read lists; single-source pinned strings) — ship with a future release if the user wants them.
- src/tools/brain/.aide body (Context/Strategy/examples) is stale vs the revised frontmatter and needs a strategist pass.
- A draft path equal to the project root yields reason "cannot read  (EISDIR)" with an empty path.
- The draft unreadable-file wording differs from the host check's labels (allowed by the brief, but inconsistent).
- The launcher-region logic is duplicated between readTemplateLauncher and upgrade's locateFrontmatter.
- The marker line format is spelled out in SKILL.md (drift risk if the format changes).
- aide_scaffold type=plan writes a `description:` field that plan-aide.md forbids (and the todo template has had a similar mismatch); fix the templates or the doc.
- Offer the new kanban-index section to this repo's brain.aide through /aide:brain config after the next release (task `ship-never-truncate-slug-rule-in-brain-template`).
- Brain note coding-playbook/study-playbook uses ### headings where the template uses ## (cosmetic; reseed or leave).
- Backlog candidate: running /aide:upgrade without a target when the pin is ahead of the running server still prescribes pinning back to the running version (existing behavior).
- Backlog candidate: a prerelease npm `latest` dist-tag would yield versionsBehind 0 in aide_info (cosmetic).
- Maintainers still sometimes call aide_cleanup without `path` first (seen again 2026-10-26).

session.aide is rewritten, never deleted (decision 18).

## Process discipline (permanent)

- One implementor per numbered plan step.
- Prose never goes through the pipeline — agent instructions, methodology docs, README and wording-only text changes are edited directly by the main agent; only behavior-changing code is pipelined (user, 2026-10-09).
- Pause for user approval before the build.
- Every /aide session checks the board at boot and keeps the feature's tasks and `## Kanban` links current.
- Record the work in session.aide in full (decision 23); stash into tasks alongside.
- Cleanup of plan/todo/brief goes through aide_cleanup via aide-maintainer.
- Release process (user, 2026-10-11), done by the agent every time it publishes: check `git status` (publish.mjs commits everything staged) → publish and confirm the Publish workflow and npm version → `npm i -g @aidemd-mcp/server@<version>` → run a headless `claude -p` session from inside the aidemd.dev checkout that applies the drifted package-owned upgrade categories through aide_upgrade (never mcp or brain), commits `chore(aide): sync methodology to <version>` and pushes to main (the push deploys via GitHub Pages) → confirm the deploy → update session.aide. Never hand-edit the site's files from this repo's session; the headless session in the site folder does the work through aide's own tools. If it reports brainMigration, tell the user (/aide:brain config needs their consent).
- Keep session.aide up to date as you work (decision 22).
- From the release after 0.14.0 on, do NOT update the global npm install after publishing — the user tests the boot's behind/upgrade prompt on their own projects (user, 2026-10-26). The aidemd.dev sync currently runs aide from the global install (the site's aide entry is the global launcher), so ask the user how to run the site sync (e.g. switch the site to a pinned npx launch) before that release's sync.

## Open questions

- Should a [migration] entry also detect a project root holding an `intent.aide/` folder with no `.aide/` (the old rename bug's footprint) and offer to rename it back? No AIDE tool renames a folder today, so the CHANGELOG currently tells users to rename it by hand.
- Should a [migration] entry tell /aide:upgrade to find host plan.aide files with no intent spec beside them and offer to write the spec (per file, with the user)?
